    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d664">

                <pb facs="0605" n="596" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg596"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/5773: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Diplomatic Agent and Consul General at Tangier</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">White</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-10-05T14:00:00-05:00">October 5, 1940—2
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>57. Referring to Goold’s telegrams Nos. 136, 143, 145 and 147<anchor n="69"
                        xml:id="d664-f1"/> concerning an increasing control and influence exercised
                    by Germany and Italy in French Morocco the Department will appreciate receiving
                    by telegraph some more detailed examination of the extent and form which that
                    reported control and influence are taking. Such an analysis, which should be
                    prepared by you in collaboration with Casablanca, should include, in addition to
                    any facts in support of Goold’s conclusions, any opinions which may be available
                    on those conclusions from responsible sources in Morocco.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d664-f1" n="69" xml:id="d664-f1-content">
                <p>Nos. 145 and 147 not printed.</p>
